# counter harness. One force call is one energy and gradient entry.
# A repeated coordinate is cached. The refused call at the cap is not counted.
# The analytic Hessian is not a force call.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# energy_min and energy_max are the final potential values on the recorded points.
# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Fixed-cell SQNM. initial_step_size is -1e-7 and alpha_min is 1e-3. The stop is the problem force norm. The ASE wrapper constructor uses initial_step_size -0.01 and eps_subsp 1e-3. On the stiffest LJ38 start a force component is about 6.1e5, and -0.01 carries that atom past the cutoff, where the force is zero. eps_subsp 1e-3 also lets a later step leave the cutoff. eps_subsp 1e-5 keeps every archived LJ38 start bound. Morse bulk uses the same coefficients. The call goes through aseOptimizer with vc_relax false. Force calls are harness calculator evaluations. Default row: history length 10 and eps_subsp 1e-5.
